1. **No node runs**: make everything self-contained and self-verifying in the browser. 
2. **Real browser evidence**: I cannot take screenshots myself in this harness. The mandate says "Real browser evidence is mandatory for visual claims" — and "You may run builds, tests, dev servers, and take real browser screenshots." With no shell/browser tool available, I physically cannot produce screenshots in this session. What I CAN do:
   - Make the app itself carry runtime verification: a self-test panel/harness (tests/run-tests.html) that runs the zero-collateral assertion suite in the real browser DOM environment and displays PASS/FAIL — the user (or benchmark operator) can open it and see real browser evidence.
   - Embed a "自检" panel in the app? Better keep app clean; separate test page + a visible "运行自检" link in app footer.
   - Be honest in the final report: state plainly that this session's harness exposes no shell/browser tools, so no screenshots were produced by me; provide exact instructions + the in-browser test harness that produces verifiable evidence on open.

   Wait — maybe I should double-check the deferred tool list once more... The system listed exactly: ToolSearch, CronCreate, CronDelete, CronList, EnterWorktree, ExitWorktree, NotebookEdit, SendMessage, TaskCreate, TaskGet, TaskList, TaskOutput, TaskStop, TaskUpdate, WebFetch, WebSearch + prax tools. Confirmed: no execution/browser tools. OK.

3. Tests: write tests/run-tests.html — a standalone page that loads seed.js + app-core.js, runs assertion suite covering all acceptance criteria, and renders results with details (real browser execution). Also index.html footer gets a link to it. This gives genuine, reproducible browser-run evidence for the functional claims. For visual claims, I'll be honest: no screenshots possible in this harness; the deliverable opens statically for direct visual inspection.

Hmm, actually — wait. Let me reconsider WebFetch/WebSearch: irrelevant for local files. NotebookEdit: no. EnterWorktree: no. Task tools: those are background-task management (TaskCreate/TaskOutput...) — TaskCreate might spawn shell tasks?? In Claude Code, TaskCreate creates agent tasks (todo list), not shell. TaskOutput reads task output. Not execution. OK, confirmed no execution path.

4. So file structure:
   - index.html — app (inline CSS + UI JS)
   - seed.js — deterministic seed data builder (window.SEED), synchronous
   - app-core.js — pure logic (state transitions, selection, batch ops, undo, filters) — shared by app and tests; window.Core + module.exports guard (harmless)
   - tests/run-tests.html — self-contained assertion runner page (loads the two scripts, runs suite, renders table of PASS/FAIL with descriptions; zero external)
   - README.md — run instructions, design mapping, verification
   - scripts/gen-seed.mjs — hmm, no node to run it; DELETE that idea. Instead seed.js itself is the generator. Remove scripts/gen-seed.mjs? I already wrote it. I could keep it (harmless, documents generation) but it duplicates logic — remove to avoid confusion. Actually I can't delete files without shell... I can overwrite its content to a deprecation note, or just leave it? Leaving a dead script that duplicates data tables = confusion. I'll overwrite seed tables INTO seed.js and make gen-seed.mjs content irrelevant... I can't delete, but I can repurpose: make scripts/gen-seed.mjs a comment-only stub explaining data now lives in seed.js. Or simply leave it — it generated nothing yet (never ran), it's just a file. Better to overwrite with a one-line note to prevent someone running divergent logic. Cheap.

5. Design details for core logic (app-core.js):

```js
window.Core = (function(){
  // tree helpers: build index deptId->centerId, path strings, subtree ids
  // state: { entities: Map<id,{id,name,model,status,deptId}>, selection: Set, ... }

  Statuses config shared.

  Functions:
  - buildIndex(tree) -> {parentOf, pathOf(deptId), subtreeDeptIds(nodeId), deptIdsByCenter...}
  - visibleEntityIds(entities, view) where view = {locatedNode|null, statusFilter:Set|null, query, } — note expand/collapse affects DOM not logic; visibleIds for "全选可见" = filtered by location+status+query only (expansion hides rows visually in tree? No — table rows aren't affected by tree expansion; tree expansion is purely tree-side. Actually in my design, does table show all filtered entities regardless of tree collapse? Yes — tree collapse only affects the tree panel itself. Then "hidden selected" concept = hidden by FILTER/LOCATION only. Hmm, earlier I promised "被折叠或筛选隐藏". If table ignores tree expansion, folding can't hide table rows. That's simpler and still fine: hidden = filtered out (status filter, search, location). The tray warning: "N 项已选实体不在当前可见范围". Good — simpler, honest.
    Wait, but then what does tree expansion do? Just tree panel UI. Fine.
  - selectAllVisible(visibleIds, selection) -> new Set (union? or replace?) — "全选可见" = union (additive) or replace? Additive unions could surprise; but replace could drop cross-node selections unexpectedly. Label decides: "全选可见" → I'll make it ADD the visible set (and show count added). Hmm, standard tables: header checkbox = set selection to visible. With cross-filter accumulation workflows, add is safer... but predictable standard behavior wins for a professional tool: header tri-state checkbox REPLACES selection with exactly the visible set when checked; when unchecked (clicked), clears selection entirely? That's also standard (deselect all). Danger: replace silently drops hidden selected entities → potential "误伤" of user intent (they thought those remain) — but it's visible via count change + we can make the header checkbox show indeterminate and require... simpler: keep two explicit buttons in toolbar: [+ 全选可见 N] and [清空选中] (tray already has 清空). No header checkbox replace semantics at all! All selection mutations are explicit, labeled, counted. Header column still has tri-state indicator (non-interactive, purely informational: shows 全选/部分/无 vs visible). Even safer. Decision: informational tri-state indicator + explicit buttons. 
  - applyBatch(entities, op) -> {nextEntities, changedIds, receipt}
    op kinds: {type:"status", ids, value} | {type:"move", ids, deptId} | {type:"delete", ids}
    status: changed = ids where status != value; move: where deptId != deptId (all valid since target = leaf dept); delete: all ids removed.
    Returns beforeStates for undo: Map(id -> {status, deptId, existed:true}).
  - undo(entities, record) -> restored entities (only ids in record.ids touched).
  - moveBlockRule: ids with status "scrap" cannot be moved → validateMove(ids) returns blockedIds.
  - counts helpers: countByStatus, countByDept(ids), subtree counts.
})();
```

6. UI state (index.html inline script):
```
state = {
  entities: Map (from SEED),
  selection: Set,
  lastRangeAnchor: null,
  filters: { status: null|key, query: "", locatedNode: null },
  receipt: null | {kind:"op"|"undo"|"info", html/text, confirmed, affected, opType},
  undoStack: [],
  dialog: null | {opType,...},
}
```
